.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "August 2026" "Simple Shell" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
simple_shell - a simple UNIX command interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simple_shell
is a simple UNIX command interpreter written in C.

It reads commands from the standard input, searches for executable programs using the
.B PATH
environment variable, creates a child process, and executes the requested command.

The shell can be used in both interactive and non-interactive modes.

.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
In interactive mode, the shell displays a prompt and waits for the user to enter a command.

Example:
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
($) /bin/ls
($) /bin/pwd
($) exit
.fi

.SH NON-INTERACTIVE MODE
The shell can read commands from standard input.

Example:
.PP
.nf
$ echo "/bin/ls" | ./hsh
.fi

.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell.

.TP
.B env
Displays the current environment variables.

.SH COMMAND EXECUTION
The shell uses the
.B PATH
environment variable to locate executable programs.

It creates a new process using
.B fork()
and executes the command in the child process using
.B execve().
The parent process waits for the child process to finish using
.B wait().

.SH ENVIRONMENT
The shell uses the environment inherited from its parent process.

.SH EXIT STATUS
The shell returns the exit status of the last executed command.

